  "title": "Shen Kuo",
  "summary": "A Song-dynasty scholar-official born in Hangzhou in 1031 who was put in charge of the Bureau of Astronomy in 1072. His book Dream Pool Essays, dated 1088, covers fields from astronomy to metallurgy and describes the magnetic compass needle. One source places the writing at Runzhou, today Zhenjiang; he died in 1095.",
